{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/371889-risen-vs-vampires-as-in-what-s-the-better-undead-to-play-as","id":371889,"title":"Risen vs Vampires (As in what's the better \"Undead\" to play as?)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-15T22:28:15-08:00","id":371889,"title":"Risen vs Vampires (As in what's the better \"Undead\" to play as?)","content":"Hello everyone, I got a question for everyone I've been wondering about recently...<br /> <br /> What Undead splat do you prefer playing as? Vampire or Risen and why?<br /> <br /> Since apparently, it seems Risen have the upper hand because they don't have numerous weaknesses Vampires have such as the beast, can walk in sunlight, don't have Jyhad politics nor are they shoehorned into inherit backstabbers/usurpers (which is also part of the Vampire curse), and even though they don't even require blood either they need patheos to fuel their powers instead and can even learn vampire disciplines as well. Although I also wonder how different playing as a Risen than a Vampire and if anyone enjoys playing as one more than the other...<br /> <br /> and lastly the biggest advantage is that Risen don't have to worry about the effects of Gehenna such as the Withering and such.<br /> <br /> Thoughts on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 01-16-2015, 01:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T22:49:00-08:00","id":371927,"title":"","content":"They are two completely different beasts tho they do often, due to the efforts of the Puppeteers Guild, gravitate towards the same circles. I'd say it's a matter of taste and character concept, some concepts work better as Vampires others as Risen.<br /> <br /> Do note that while lacking the more commonly known Vampiric weaknesses they do have some of their own.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires have such as the beast </div> </div> </div>And Risen have Shadows who are usually somewhat empowered by the experience of Rising and the greater ease to follow up on their Dark Passions on the Skinlands. In comparison the Beast is generally considerably smaller issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can walk in sunlight </div> </div> </div>But are still more dead than Vampires, no way to mimic life and such. But it is nice to feel the sun again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> don't have Jyhad politics </div> </div> </div>If they take the Guilds advice and masquerade as Vampires they kinda are drawn into the Jyhad politics by default. But just like Vampires they can try to avoid it by staying away from other Undead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> nor are they shoehorned into inherit backstabbers/usurpers </div> </div> </div>But thanks to their Shadows they are extremely unpredictable and likely to end up backstabbing someone/everyone at some point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> even though they don't even require blood either they need patheos to fuel their powers </div> </div> </div>True, and this does make it a bit easier on them as they do not need to attack humans to refuel their batteries but only to follow their Passions and be around people with strong emotions. But this is also a huge thematic difference between them and Vampires as they are seemingly less harmful parasites than the Vampires and it makes it easier for them to hide from hunters, htough them being a bit deader than Vampires and unable to mimic life to such extents tends to make up for that particular difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> can even learn vampire disciplines as well </div> </div> </div>Only the three physicals and Obfuscate though and while similar to disciplines they technically aren't quite them but close enough to teach them crosssplats anyhow.<br /> <br /> But all in all it is quite a different experience due to Risen being dominated by their Passions and having things they do need to protect, Fetters and Conduit, and the difference in parasitism between them and Vampires. I kinda lean towards Risen, but that is because Wraith is my favourite line, but still I stay with my earlier opinion that it is largely concept driven choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T23:03:08-08:00","id":371964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/371889-risen-vs-vampires-as-in-what-s-the-better-undead-to-play-as?p=371927#post371927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But thanks to their Shadows they are extremely unpredictable and likely to end up backstabbing someone/everyone at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh....well I guess I have to find another undead to play as then because this is highly problematic for me which as you can see I reject any forced inherit notion of &quot;backstabbing&quot; which once you think about it especially them have to avoid each other so they won't kill each other which is nice way of prolonging a species if they can't cooperate which they might as well be long dead..<br /> <br /> I think this is where the biggest problem with games like VTM and now here lie....<br /> <br /> To explain this better, sure I don't mind if Vampires or Undead can backstab/Usurp power which is not the problem, but rather the main problem lies that they're <i>forced</i> to do it due to some 'curse' or something which deprives them making a choice to do it or not or even having their own reasons why they choose to do it but nope it's like a quick &quot;You have outlasted your usefulness&quot; without any reason at all and they either get whacked or leads to a fight of roaring rampage of revenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","user":"DeathPathoes","date":". 01-16-2015, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1997-deathpathoes","name":"DeathPathoes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T00:21:11-08:00","id":372066,"title":"","content":"Well to be honest the backstabbing happening here, with Risen and Wraith in general, is usually that of the Shadow backstabbing it's Psyche though that can and often does involve fouling Psyche's relationships unless said relations are something the Shadow can use. And how, if and when all depend upon the Shadows nature and Dark Passions so it isn't necessarily given though it is likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T20:14:52-08:00","id":373988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DeathPathoes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/371889-risen-vs-vampires-as-in-what-s-the-better-undead-to-play-as?p=371964#post371964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh....well I guess I have to find another undead to play as then because this is highly problematic for me which as you can see I reject any forced inherit notion of &quot;backstabbing&quot; which once you think about it especially them have to avoid each other so they won't kill each other which is nice way of prolonging a species if they can't cooperate which they might as well be long dead..<br /> <br /> I think this is where the biggest problem with games like VTM and now here lie....<br /> <br /> To explain this better, sure I don't mind if Vampires or Undead can backstab/Usurp power which is not the problem, but rather the main problem lies that they're <i>forced</i> to do it due to some 'curse' or something which deprives them making a choice to do it or not or even having their own reasons why they choose to do it but nope it's like a quick &quot;You have outlasted your usefulness&quot; without any reason at all and they either get whacked or leads to a fight of roaring rampage of revenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole &quot;backstabbing&quot; notion is a flawed understanding of Catharsis. A wraith (or Risen)'s shadow is their &quot;road not travelled&quot;, the repressed urges and emotions given &quot;life&quot;/form by death. The shadow may not like the main personality's friends/goals, but it has its own fish to fry. . . and thus screwing them over (or destroying them) isn't usually the first priority.<br /> <br /> That being said, a wraith's shadow isn't exactly &quot;nice and friendly&quot;. Most are psychotic and vindictive, driven to pursue goals the wraith deemed monstrous in life. But its not stupid, either. It can pretend to be the wraith's normal personality (if it has to), although close friends will notice that the wraith suddenly seems to be angrier, crueler, and more violent than usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-17T20:48:00-08:00","id":374030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole &quot;backstabbing&quot; notion is a flawed understanding of Catharsis. </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. I did say they are <i>likely</i> to end up backstabbing their friends not that they will, in my second post I did clarify that the backstabbing here is mostly that of the Psyche, even the most benevolent of Shadows seeks to undermine the Psyche either to take them both to Oblivion or to take over the shared Corpus this by it's very definition means backstabbing it's Psyche, unless that Psyche also want's these things to happen which would be rather unlikely. I also mentioned it depending upon the Shadows Nature and Dark Passions. And about the Shadows stupidity... it's either just as stupid as it's Psyche or considerably smarter, should it have the appropriate Thorn.<br /> <br /> But no it's not a flawed understanding of Catharsis at all. Most of the time Shadow may find it most useful to keep the Psyche's relationships as they are, colored by their Dark Passions, but should any of them conflict with it's goals it will take measures appropriate to it's Nature to dispose of that obstacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T10:49:22-08:00","id":380295,"title":"","content":"In regards to the 'backstabbing' requirement, neither game outright DEMANDS it, as a matter of fact. Sure, it's a quick path of drama, but there's nothing that says the Beast forces vampires to eat each other. The Beast winds up being the excuse that many Kindred use for following their worst urges, just as you or I may say, 'the Devil made me do it.' <b>*</b><br /> <br /> The thing I see as the biggest difference between the two isn't mechanical, but rather it is one of society. Even if you choose to say that the Sixth Great Maelstrom booted huge numbers of ghosts into the Skinlands to become Risen, they won't find any kind of structured social system for their on this side of the Shroud no matter how many appear. The vampires, on the other hand, have had millennia to build their society of Clans and Sects and the Jyhad and whathaveyou. The Risen may either cling to the social structures of the Underworld or try to blend in with humanity (or the vampires as the case may be), but they don't have anything to call their own beyond that of a very small scale. Perhaps a gang or <i>ad hoc</i> familial group of Risen come together, but they never quite fit into any place of their own.<br /> <br /> ...As stated above, it really depends on what you want of course. I tend to see the Risen as having a necessarily limited time in the world, as they are driven by Passions and goaded by the Shadow, it's an existence that leads to ruin \u2013 or drama, if you like. Please don't take that as how it must be played, though, as mileage always and ever varies, and it's your game.<br /> <br /> <b>*</b> Not to presume what any of you might ACTUALLY say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}